      'watches twice.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The written record',
    detail:
      'Architecture note, health report, submission record, ticket history — whichever of them ' +
      'your engagement produced.',
  },
];

// Seven service cells and one that is not a service. The eighth fills the
// second row of a four-across grid, which a seven-item set would otherwise
// leave ragged, and it earns the space: the commonest state a reader
// arrives in is not knowing which of the seven is theirs.
const contents = [
  ...ENGAGEMENTS.map((e) => ({
    n: e.n,
    title: e.name,
    href: `#${e.id}`,
    blurb: e.contents,
  })),
  {
    n: '→',
    title: 'Not sure which?',
    href: '#route-heading',
    blurb: 'Say the problem out loud — the table below has a row for it',
  },
];

const servicesSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type':    'ItemList',
  name:       'CloudAlgo Services',
  url:        'https://cloudalgo.com/services',
  itemListElement: ENGAGEMENTS.map((e, i) => ({
    '@type':  'ListItem',
    position: i + 1,
    name:     bySlug.get(e.slug)!.data.title,
    url:      `https://cloudalgo.com/services/${e.slug}`,
  })),
};
---
<Page
  title="Services — seven engagements, and what each one ends with | CloudAlgo"
  description="Salesforce consulting, AppExchange product development, MuleSoft integration and RPA, AWS architecture, Airflow pipelines and a support retainer. How long each runs, what it involves, and what you keep."
  schema={servicesSchema}
>
  <PageMasthead
    crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Services' }]}
    facts={[
      { term: 'Engagements', detail: '7' },
      { term: 'Platforms',   detail: 'Salesforce · MuleSoft · AWS' },
      { term: 'Delivered',   detail: '70+ projects' },
      { term: 'Smallest',    detail: '10 hrs / month' },
      { term: 'Emergency',   detail: 'Unlimited P1, every tier' },
      { term: 'Proven by',   detail: 'OrgVitals · Pledgivo · AlgoBridge' },
      { term: 'Enquiries',   detail: 'contact@cloudalgo.com' },
    ]}
  >
    <Fragment slot="title">
      Seven engagements. You end up <span class="mark mark--draw">owning it</span>, every time.
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="lede">
      Six of the seven end with the repository, the runbook and a session with your admins. The
      seventh is a retainer you can stop the month it stops earning its place. Either way, nothing
      we leave behind needs us on call to keep running.
    </Fragment>
  </PageMasthead>

  <ContentsBar items={contents} label="Services" class="contents-bar--8 anim-fade-up" />

  <section class="section-press" aria-labelledby="shapes-heading">
    <div class="section-press__head anim-fade-up">
      <h2 id="shapes-heading" class="section-title section-title--xs section-title--tighter section-press__title">
        Seven shapes, drawn to scale.
      </h2>
      <span class="section-press__note">Six months, left to right</span>
    </div>

    <ServiceSchedule
      class="anim-fade-up"
      axis={['Month 0', '01', '02', '03', '04', '05', '06']}
      rows={ENGAGEMENTS.map((e) => ({
        n: e.n,
        name: e.name,
        shape: e.shape,
        href: `#${e.id}`,
        bar: e.bar,
        roll: e.roll,
      }))}
      caption="six of the seven end, and the ember mark is that ending — repository, runbook, admin session. The seventh is a retainer, and runs until you stop it. Lengths are typical, not contractual."
    />
  </section>

  <section class="section-press" aria-labelledby="engagements-heading">
    <div class="section-press__head anim-fade-up">
      <h2 id="engagements-heading" class="section-title section-title--xs section-title--tighter section-press__title">
        What each one actually involves.
      </h2>
      <span class="section-press__note">Scope, sequence and terms</span>
    </div>

    {ENGAGEMENTS.map((e) => (
      <ServiceSpread
        class="anim-fade-up"
        id={e.id}
        n={e.n}
        name={e.name}
        shape={e.stamp.shape}
        proof={proofStamp.get(e.slug) ?? e.stamp.note}
        tagline={e.tagline}
        lead={e.lead}
        track={e.track}
        ending={e.ending}
        caveat={e.caveat}
        stackLabel={e.stackLabel}
        stack={e.stack}
        terms={e.terms}
        actions={[
          { label: `${e.cta} →`, href: '/contact/', primary: true },
          { label: 'Read the full scope', href: `/services/${e.slug}/` },
        ]}
      >
        {e.id === 'support' && (
          <SlaWindows slot="detail" windows={WINDOWS}>
            <b>Initial response, written into the contract</b> — not the sales deck. Unlimited P1
            on Essentials, Growth and Enterprise alike.
          </SlaWindows>
        )}
      </ServiceSpread>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="section-press" aria-labelledby="route-heading">
    <div class="section-press__head anim-fade-up">
      <h2 id="route-heading" class="section-title section-title--xs section-title--tighter section-press__title">
        Start here if this is you.
      </h2>
      <span class="section-press__note">Eight symptoms, one row each</span>
    </div>

    <RouteTable
      class="anim-fade-up"
      corner="On the call"
      destination="Where that goes"
      rows={ROUTES}
      caption="Common problems and which engagement handles each one."
    >
      <p class="compare-note anim-fade-up" slot="footnote">
        One answer is the same in every row: the first call is about your org, not our engagement
        types. We do not publish rates — the number comes after that call, once there is a scope to
        put one against. If none of the seven fits, we will say so and point you at whoever does it
        properly.
      </p>
    </RouteTable>
  </section>

  <ClosingManifest
    class="anim-fade-up"
    labelledby="manifest-heading"
    kicker="The last week of every engagement"
    items={MANIFEST}
  >
    <Fragment slot="title">Owning it is a checklist, not a promise.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="note">
      Seven shapes, one ending. Whichever of them you buy, the closing week is the same four items,
      and none of them needs us on call afterwards. That is the test we build against — and the
      reason three of the seven are proven by software we run ourselves.
    </Fragment>
    <a class="btn btn-light btn-sm" slot="actions" href="/case-studies/">Read the case studies &rarr;</a>
  </ClosingManifest>

</Page>
